ished by Kublai (Emperor Shizu or Setsen Khan), the fifth khagan-emperor of the Mongol Empire from the Borjigin clan, and lasted from 1271 to 1368 CE. In Chinese history, the Yuan dynasty followed the Song dynasty and preceded the Ming dynasty.\nAlthough Genghis Khan's enthronement as khagan in 1206 was described in Chinese as the Han-style title of emperor and the Mongol Empire had ruled territories including modern-day northern China for decades, it was not until 1271 that Kublai Khan officially proclaimed the dynasty in the traditional Han style, and the conquest was not complete until 1279 when the Southern Song dynasty was defeated in the Battle of Yamen. His realm was, by this point, isolated from the other Mongol-led khanates and controlled most of modern-day China and its surrounding areas, including modern-day Mongolia."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q101186473","value_label":"Khanbaliq","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Khanbaliq"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q7850","value_label":"Chinese","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Chinese"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q9246","value_label":"Mongolian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Mongolian"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q483889","value_label":"Tibetan Buddhism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tibetan Buddhism"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q9581","value_label":"Confucianism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Confucianism"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q9598","value_label":"Taoism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Taoism"},{"qid":"Q7313","kind":"off